# Diagnosing annotation reports

Look at the data before the code. OData is read-only and needs no login; use it for every volume a report names.

- Base URL: `https://websvc.codepharm.net/<Volume>/OData/` (`RC1`, `RC2`, ...). Never write to it; it is a protected
  production service.
- One structure: `Structures(<id>)` (TypeID, ParentID, Label, Username, Created).
- Its children: `Structures?$filter=ParentID eq <id>`.
- Its links: `StructureLinks?$filter=SourceID eq <id> or TargetID eq <id>`.
- Type names: `StructureTypes(<TypeID>)`.

Link refusals (`StructureLinkViewModelBase.IsValidStructureLinkTarget`, `ViewModel/StructureLink.cs`): the client
refuses, with no message, a link to itself, a link that already exists, and any link between a structure and one of its
ancestors (the check walks both parent chains). The usual cause of "this one won't link" is a child created under the
wrong parent (e.g. a glial adjacency placed from the synapse's location, so the synapse is its parent); the fix is to
change the child's parent.
